# fix2 (critic shards03 2nd round): VOID RESCUE. A shard world's one SpawnProvider is the Farming hub, painted only when Farming is
# entered, so a player of another shard who fell and died respawned over the void and fell again (a loop until /hub). Now a member
# below RESCUE_Y (20 under the island surface; islands are 3 deep, the engine kills at y -32) is caught by the 1 s sweep: back to the
# hub of the region they are over when that shard is placed + owned, else the first placed + owned shard (Farming first); the region
# is PAINTED first (ShFill.region -> ShHop), so an unpainted region is never the target. No placed shard = the island hub.
# One rescue per player per 4 s (the paint + teleport take a moment). -1 = nothing to do, -2 = the island hub, else the shard kind.
